Nyxus Suxyn — live ISO hardware rules
=====================================

This stick is for ANYONE's PC. The machine that baked it is only the
build host. Do not clone that chassis into the image.

LIVE ISO (this squashfs)
------------------------
- Stock Arch `linux`. Never localmodconfig. Never strip modules.
- Full `linux-firmware` (Intel / NVIDIA / AMD / Atheros / Realtek / …).
  Do not drop blobs because the baker's laptop does not use them.
- Live initramfs MODULES: common GPU set
    i915 amdgpu nvidia nvidia_modeset nvidia_drm
  or empty + no autodetect. NEVER the baker's
  /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/20-nyxus-hardware.conf
  (that file is AMD iGPU + NVIDIA dGPU on one Alienware).
- Hyprland monitors: `monitor = , preferred, auto, 1`
  NEVER `eDP-1, 1920x1200@165`.
- GPU env (LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME, __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME) is decided at
  session start from this machine's GPUs. Not an NVIDIA-only default.
- Live user is `nyx`. Calamares creates the real user. Never `gowski`.
- Hostname is `suxyn`. Never the baker's hostname.
- No Wi-Fi secrets, no weather lat/lon, no Brain/notes.

INSTALLED SYSTEM (after Calamares, or first boot)
-------------------------------------------------
- nyxus-hwdetect reads THAT machine's PCI bus and writes
  /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/20-nyxus-hardware.conf
- Calamares shellprocess@initramfs runs hwdetect, then mkinitcpio -P
- First boot runs /etc/nyxus-firstboot.d/03-hardware-initramfs.sh
  (no-op on live: /run/archiso is present)
- nyxus-hwcaps drives Settings ▸ Hardware (hide fans if none)

This file is the on-image copy of the baker's hard rules.
